   "GuideTutorialPage_3612702_Content": "After obtaining a Collection Item, equip it from your Backpack or Utility.",
   "GuideTutorialPage_3612703_Content": "Once a Collection Item is equipped, you can summon and interact with it in the overworld.",
   "GuideTutorialPage_36127_Content": "Collection Items are a rare type of special item.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3612802_Content": "Every run is a race against the clock. Your remaining time ticks down continuously, and certain actions can either add or cost you time. When the timer hits 0, your run is over.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36128_Content": "In this event, you'll venture through the Dreamfield across a series of Marchstones, clearing the Nodes within each Marchstone in order.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3612902_Content": "Equip Sediments to gain new abilities for your run.\nAlong with passive effects, Sediments also grant Active Skills you can trigger in combat. Each Active Skill has a cooldown and a limited number of uses per Marchstone, so save them for the right moment.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36129_Content": "In this event, select one Resonator to act as your Primary Resonator. The Primary Resonator will be enhanced with new abilities and stat boosts.\nTake Carlotta as an example:\nWhen Carlotta is in the <color=Highlight>Twilight Tango</color> state, casting <color=Highlight>Resonance Skill</color> resets the charges of <color=Highlight>Death Knell</color>.\nCasting <color=Highlight>Death Knell</color> while in <color=Highlight>Twilight Tango</color> deals extra Vibration Strength DMG to enemy targets.\n<color=Highlight>Resonance Liberation: Fatal Finale</color> deals more DMG to immobilized targets.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3613002_Content": "As your Team Level rises, your Primary Resonator unlocks powerful, unique buffs. Check the Team Details screen to see what they do.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3613003_Content": "{Cus:Ipt,Touch=Tap PC=Click Gamepad=Select} a Resonator's avatar to see the Team Level buffs for each Resonator.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36130_Content": "Your Resonators gain stronger buffs as your Team Level rises. Clearing certain Marchstones automatically levels up your team, and that level carries over even when you swap Resonators.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3613102_Content": "Chrono Rings appear along the path between certain combat areas. Pass through them to add a little extra time to the clock.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36131_Content": "In some Nodes, enemies are split across multiple combat areas. Once you clear one area, head to the next to keep fighting.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3613202_Content": "The more rows or columns you clear at a time, the more bonus points you get.\nReach the target score to clear the stage.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36132_Content": "Drag and rotate the blocks to fill the empty space. Complete a full row or column to clear the blocks and earn points.\nNew blocks will be supplied on the right side once the current set is used up.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36133_Content": "Damaged Data Blocks cannot be cleared, but completing the rows or columns that contain them can still clear the other standard blocks.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36134_Content": "Drag and rotate the blocks to fill the empty space. Complete a full row or column to clear blocks.\nClear the blocks containing Medals to collect them.\nCollect a set number of Medals to clear the stage.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36135_Content": "Clearing a Blast Block blasts away all blocks in a 3x3 area around it (except Damaged Data Blocks).\nWhenever the blocks on the right refresh, there's a chance for Blast Blocks to appear.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36136_Content": "Some blocks are glitched and cannot be cleared directly.\nTier-1 Glitched Blocks take 1 clear to repair, after which you can clear them like normal blocks.\nA Blast Block on a Glitched Block won't detonate until the glitch is repaired and the block is cleared.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36137_Content": "Clearing a Super Blast Block blasts away all blocks in a 5x5 area around it (except Damaged Data Blocks).\nWhenever the blocks on the right refresh, there's a small chance for Super Blast Blocks to appear.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36138_Content": "Some blocks are glitched and cannot be cleared directly.\nTier-2 Glitched Blocks take 2 clears to repair.\nOnce fixed, you can clear them like normal blocks.\nA Blast Block on a Glitched Block won't detonate until the glitch is repaired and the block is cleared.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3613902_Content": "When your Fatigue reaches a certain level, event success rates and the stats gained from activities decrease.\nWhen your Fatigue reaches an even higher level, you cannot perform any activities that increase Fatigue.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3613903_Content": "When your Fatigue is high, perform Break activities to reduce it.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36139_Content": "Activities in your schedule can either increase or reduce Fatigue, depending on their type.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3614002_Content": "There are five stats you can develop: Knowledge, Thinking, Aesthetics, Physique, and Feeling.\nKnowledge and Thinking relate to academic growth and can be improved through Student Council activities.\nAesthetics and Physique relate to growth in arts and sports and can be improved through Club Association activities.\nFeeling relates to the story and can be increased through certain story choices.\nFocus on developing the highlighted stats according to your story choices.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_3614003_Content": "Increase your stats through story choices and activities.\nRepeat the same activity to level it up, increasing the stats it grants.\nOnce certain activities reach Lv. 3, keep completing them a certain number of times to unlock their corresponding Advanced Activities.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36140_Content": "Build your stats and make choices throughout a year of school life to unlock different endings.",
+  "GuideTutorialPage_36141_Content": "Keep playing in Infinite Mode until you fail, and score as many points as you can.\nTo earn rewards of Infinite Mode, simply reach the required points, then exit and finalize your result.",
   "GuideTutorialPage_36_Content": "An error occurred. Please contact our Customer Service for assistance",
