   "HelpText_66_Title": "Chord Cleansing",
   "HelpText_670_Content": "[About]\nThe Ivory Gatekeeper has sent you an SOS over WavesLine! The gate in the depths of the Somnoire—the one that should never be opened, the one you once shut—has somehow come open again. Now, terrifying Nightmares are once again running rampant in the Somnoire...\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 22. Activate the Four Chime Shaftpost during Main Quest \"The Wind Before the Storm.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. In this challenge, you can choose \"Support Echoes\" to assist you in battle, greatly enhancing the combat abilities of Resonators.\n2. Downed Resonators will automatically revive after a while.\n3. This event can be played in Co-Op Mode.\n4. Only designated Echoes can be used in this event (Sonatas remain effective; only the main Echo Skill is replaced).\n5. Surface Layer Stage Points: Clearance Points + (Remaining Time x Time Coefficient).\n6. Clear all Surface Layer stages to unlock the Abyss of the Final Dreams for a boss-rush challenge.\n7. Total Points are the sum of the highest points from the Surface Layer stages and the Abyss of the Final Dreams (Deep Layer stages other than the Abyss of the Final Dreams do not have points).",
   "HelpText_670_Title": "New Event \"If Dreams Still Reverberate\" is now available!",
+  "HelpText_673_Content": "About Second Solaris School",
+  "HelpText_673_Title": "Second Solaris School",
   "HelpText_676_Content": "[About]\nThe latest flagship offering from Second Coming of Solaris! Come experience the fun of tapping Echo Pieces away!\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. During the event, stages become available daily.\n2. Each stage has two difficulties: Easy and Hard. Complete the Easy difficulty to unlock the Hard challenge.\n3. Complete the goals of each stage to earn rewards.\n\n[Instructions]\n1. Swap Echo Pieces across the board to line up three or more of the same type to clear them.\n2. Clearing Pieces earns points and charges the Resonator's Skill Energy.\n3. Once Skill Energy reaches the required amount, the Resonator's Skill will trigger automatically, unleashing a powerful effect.\n4. Matching more than three Pieces at once creates a special Bonus Piece.\n5. Some stages feature special Pieces with unique effects that require specific methods to clear.\n6. Reach the Stage Goal within the given move limit to clear the stage.",
   "HelpText_676_Title": "Echo Erase",
   "HelpText_677_Content": "[About]\nLisha, apprentice Artisan, reporting for duty!\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14 and activate the Four Chime Shaftpost during Main Quest Chapter IV Act I \"The Wind Before the Storm.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. During the event, you will enter a special Sonoro Sphere to battle waves of enemies within a set time limit, with the aid of unique buffs.\n2. You collect Coins by dealing damage to enemies, and lose Coins when taking damage.\n3. Advancing through enemy waves unlocks more special buffs to give you the support you need.\n4. Clearing a wave grants bonus time. The Coins you have collected by the end of the countdown will be your Coins record for this stage.",
@@ -94007,27 +103055,63 @@
   "HelpText_682_Title": "Cubie Wars Collection",
   "HelpText_689_Content": "Cubie Wars illustrated tutorial description",
   "HelpText_689_Title": "Cubie Wars illustrated tutorial",
+  "HelpText_690_Content": "[About]\nIn the Dreamfield Odyssey event, you can select 1 Primary Resonator and 2 Secondary Resonators to take on a series of challenges. The event consists of multiple Marchstones, each containing several Nodes. At the start of each Marchstone, you can choose which Sediment to bring into battle.\nThe remaining time continuously counts down during each challenge. Defeating enemies and performing certain actions in combat grant extra time. The more time you have left when you complete the challenge, the higher your Rating will be.\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. Select 1 Primary Resonator and 2 Secondary Resonators to take on the challenge. Secondary Resonators have limited Vigor, and each Marchstone you enter uses some of it.\n2. Clear specific Nodes to level up your Resonators and Echoes. Leveling up strengthens their abilities and boosts certain stats.\n3. You start with a set number of Sediments and can obtain more by clearing designated Nodes. Sediments grant Active Skills that can be used in combat.\n4. Perform various actions in combat to earn additional time. The challenge ends when the remaining time reaches 0. Defeat enemies as quickly as possible while earning additional time to keep the challenge going.\n5. Players are ranked separately for each Primary Resonator based on clear times. Check your percentile on the server leaderboard, as well as your ranking among friends.\n6. The same Weapon or Echo can't be equipped by two different Resonators at once. You can't start a challenge if any Resonator has a Weapon or Echo equipped that another recorded Resonator has already used in your current save.",
+  "HelpText_690_Title": "Dreamfield Odyssey",
   "HelpText_691_Content": "[About]\nFollowing the resolution of anomalies of the Simulacrum Nexus, a mysterious girl sends you a WavesLine message, claiming she \"has a favor to ask.\" As the matter unfolds, a story about Hsin the Moon Fox, the past Sentinel, comes to light.\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14 and complete the Main Quest \"Simulacrum of the Heart: Epilogue.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\nComplete the Tales Quest \"Moonlike Heart, Mortal Longing\" to claim the quest rewards. The event will close after Version 3.7 ends. In versions after 3.7, if you meet the quest unlock conditions, you can still accept and complete this quest from the quest page to claim its rewards.",
   "HelpText_691_Title": "Moonlike Heart, Mortal Longing",
+  "HelpText_693_Content": "[About]\nA huge update just hit \"Lahai-Roi Blocks\"—the long-awaited rotate feature is finally here! And it looks like there are more hidden mechanics in store than meets the eye...\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n[Rules]\nA new stage will be unlocked each day during the event. \nEach stage has two difficulties: Normal and Hard. Finish the Normal difficulty to unlock the Hard challenge. Complete the goals of each stage to earn rewards.",
+  "HelpText_693_Title": "Lahai-Roi Blocks: Turnabout",
   "HelpText_694_Content": "Replay Mode\n1. You can replay any Main Quest you've already completed using Replay Mode.\n2. Your progress is automatically saved when you exit Replay Mode. You can resume from where you left off in the Journey Log, or reset your progress manually.\n3. You'll have a separate Backpack while in Replay Mode. Items obtained during Replay Mode only exist there and won't carry over.\n4. Some features are unavailable while in Replay Mode.",
   "HelpText_694_Title": "Replay Mode",
+  "HelpText_698_Content": "[About]\nWelcome to Second Solaris School! A brand-new school-life simulation entry in the Second Coming of Solaris series has officially launched!\nAs the train slowly pulls into the station, the platform announcement guides \"you,\" the protagonist of the story, back from a distant land to the small town where you spent your childhood. Over the course of a year at school, plan your schedule, build your skills, share everyday laughs with your friends in school, and face the challenges of growing up together as you prepare for the final evaluation and write your own Story Ending...\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14 and complete Event Quest \"Welcome to Second Coming of Solaris: Unwritten Dreams.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. Use Schedules to plan your weekly routine. Take classes, do extracurricular activities, and work part-time jobs to raise your stats and earn various rewards. Remember to schedule enough breaks to avoid getting overly fatigued.\n2. On weekends, you can freely visit different locations to chat with friends, increase your Intimacy with them, and unlock character stories. You can also accept Special Requests from your friends for generous stat progression.\n3. Midway through your school year, you can choose to join either the Student Council or the Club Association. Work side by side with your friends, enjoy a fulfilling and lively school life, and take on new trials together. As your schedule progresses, major events such as the School Anniversary, exams, club competitions, and the Coming-of-Age Ceremony will unfold one after another.\n4. Different growth paths, experiences, and story choices all lead to different Story Endings and Companion Endings. Once you meet the required conditions, you can choose a \"future\" of your own.\n5. After reaching an ending, you can start your school life anew to try different choices, unlock more story branches, and experience other Story Endings.\n\nThis is a permanent event. Starting in Version 3.8, you can access it anytime from the Events page. Any unclaimed rewards will be automatically sent to your mailbox if you log in within 30 days after the reward period.\nYou can't claim limited-time rewards once the reward window ends, but you can keep playing to earn permanent rewards.",
+  "HelpText_698_Title": "Second Coming of Solaris: Unwritten Dreams",
   "HelpText_69_Content": "1. Some Resonators have special Companion Stories, through which you get to learn all the intimate details of them.\n2. Companion Stories are unlocked when certain requirements are met. You can claim abundant rewards after completing them.",
   "HelpText_69_Title": "Companion Stories",
   "HelpText_6_Content": "<color=yellow>Character Introduction: </color>",
   "HelpText_6_Title": "Character Introduction: Taoqi",
+  "HelpText_702_Content": "Use the Schedules to plan every activity from Monday to Friday.\n\nRegular Activities: Some regular activities level up after you complete them a certain number of times, giving you more stat rewards. After certain activities reach Lv. 3, you can keep completing them to unlock their corresponding Advanced Activities.\n\nSpecial Requests: You can accept Special Requests from characters on the map. You need to first add them to Schedules before carrying them out. Special Requests will replace basic Daytime Courses and provide substantial stat rewards.\n\nThe \"Same as Last Week\" button copies last week's schedule so you can put it into action quickly.",
+  "HelpText_702_Title": "Schedules",
+  "HelpText_703_Content": "During your time at Second Solaris School, the school's Project List will gradually unlock as time goes on. The Projects available to you will also vary based on the student organization you join later on.\nCompleting Projects earns Project Points. Once you accumulate 100 Project Points, you can claim Project Rewards from your friends. Be sure to claim your rewards in time after completing a Project.\nCompleting the <color=#d19f27>Final Evaluation Project</color> in the second semester may just be the key to resolving Second Solaris School's crisis...\n\nEvery Project has a time limit. Please complete each Project before its <color=#d19f27>deadline</color>, as expired Projects can no longer be completed. Plan your time wisely and complete as many Projects as you can to earn even greater rewards!\nIf any rewards for completed Projects remain unclaimed when the deadline passes, they will be sent to your Backpack automatically.",
+  "HelpText_703_Title": "Project List",
+  "HelpText_704_Content": "<color=#de7175>Key Stats - Student Council:</color> Affect event success rate and Qualifying Exam results.\n<texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity38/SolarSchool/T_IconSolarSchoolZSA01.T_IconSolarSchoolZSA01,0.75/>Knowledge: Related location - Science Classroom.\n<texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity38/SolarSchool/T_IconSolarSchoolZSA02.T_IconSolarSchoolZSA02,0.75/>Thinking: Related location - Student Council.\n\n<color=#489eae>Key Stats - Club Association:</color> Affect event success rate and National Music Competition results.\n<texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity38/SolarSchool/T_IconSolarSchoolZSA03.T_IconSolarSchoolZSA03,0.75/>Aesthetics: Related location - Club Association.\n<texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity38/SolarSchool/T_IconSolarSchoolZSA05.T_IconSolarSchoolZSA05,0.75/>Physique: Related location - Athletic Field.\n\n<color=#d19f27>Special Stats:</color>\n<texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity38/SolarSchool/T_IconSolarSchoolZSA04.T_IconSolarSchoolZSA04,0.75/>Feeling: Affects the success rate of events. Gained through <b>Story Choices</b>. Related location: Coast.\n<texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity38/SolarSchool/T_IconSolarSchoolZSA00Renqi.T_IconSolarSchoolZSA00Renqi,0.75/>Popularity: Required to accept Special Requests. Gained through <b>Completing Special Requests</b> and <b>pressing Like on the forum</b>. Related locations: Liaison Center, Family Restaurant, School Store.\n<texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity38/SolarSchool/T_IconSolarSchoolZSA00Coin02.T_IconSolarSchoolZSA00Coin02,0.75/>School Badge: Required for purchasing items in the School Store. Gained through <b>Completing Special Requests</b>. Related locations: Liaison Center, Family Restaurant, School Store.",
+  "HelpText_704_Title": "Stats",
+  "HelpText_705_Content": "Gallery displays Story Endings, Daily Snapshots, and Theme Songs.\nExperience different story options or reach different Story Endings to unlock more content in Gallery.\nYou can also load a save before the ending to reach other Story Endings through different options and unlock the corresponding content in Gallery.",
+  "HelpText_705_Title": "Gallery",
+  "HelpText_706_Content": "[About]\nWord has it that Maji of Lollo Logistics is gearing up for a very long journey. Of course, between rounds of prep work, he hasn't forgotten his old friends, and has put together a brand-new sponsorship event.\nDuring the event, complete the daily tasks to claim Lollo Stamps in return for your favor. Lollo Stamps can be exchanged for Lollo Helper special deliveries.\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n[Event Rules]\nDuring the event, you can complete Lollo Campaigns to obtain a set number of Lollo Stamps.\nEach Lollo Stamp can be exchanged for a Lollo Helper special delivery.\nThere are 3 Inventories for the Lollo Helper special deliveries. Once you collect all deliveries in an Inventory, the next Inventory will be unlocked.\nIf you win the Lollo Express special delivery service, you can claim all deliveries in the current Inventory.\nAfter the event ends, the unfinished Lollo Campaign will not be available, and all remaining Lollo Stamps will be withdrawn.",
+  "HelpText_706_Title": "Lollo Campaign: Groundwork",
+  "HelpText_707_Title": "Gifts of Bygone Dreams",
+  "HelpText_709_Title": "Whither the Wind",
   "HelpText_70_Content": "[Standard Merge]\nYou can merge or Batch Merge 5 unupgraded Echoes into 1 random new Echo in the Terminal.\nYou cannot select equipped and locked Echoes as Merge Materials.\n\n[Targeted Merge]\nThis feature unlocks at Data Bank Lv. 15.\nYou can merge 5 unupgraded 5-Star Echoes into a random new Echo of the Sonata Effect of your choice.\nYou cannot select equipped and locked Echoes as Merge Materials.\n*If a selected Sonata Effect currently only has Cost-1 or Cost-3 Echoes unlocked, Targeted Merge may still produce an Echo of a locked Cost type. In this case, the Echo produced will be of 3-Star rarity and will unlock the corresponding Echo Collection entry. Afterward, you may obtain Echoes of the newly unlocked Cost type. The highest Rarity of the Echoes obtained will depend on the current Data Bank level.\n\n[New Echoes]\nThe Rarity of the Echo produced depends on your Data Bank level and is irrelevant to the Rarity of merged Echoes. Upgrade your Data Bank to get Echoes of higher Rarity from Data Merge.\nData Merge only produces Echoes already unlocked.\n\n[Extra Yield]\nStandard Merge sometimes produce extra Echoes in addition to the base yield.\nMerge Echoes of higher Rarity and Cost for a higher chance to yield extra Echoes.\n*Targeted Merge does not produce extra Echoes.\n\n[Auto Select]\nAuto Select lets you quickly select available Echoes in the order displayed. You can change the sort and filter settings to change which Echoes are displayed and selected first.",
   "HelpText_70_Title": "Data Merge",
+  "HelpText_710_Content": "[Server Rankings]\n1. Your best result for each Resonator will be recorded on the server leaderboard after the results are finalized. Each Resonator has its own leaderboard.\n2. The server leaderboard refreshes periodically and only displays your current percentile ranking on the server.\n3. Rankings will be finalized after a set period following the end of the event. Players in the top 20.0% can claim a special commemorative item.\n\n[Friend Rankings]\n1. Your friends' results will appear on the friend leaderboard, which only includes players who have added each other as friends.",
+  "HelpText_710_Title": "Dreamfield Odyssey Rankings",
+  "HelpText_711_Content": "[Team Level]\n1. Your team will level up after clearing specific Nodes.\n2. Leveling up your team enhances your Resonators' abilities.\n3. Primary Resonators, Support Secondary Resonators, and Healing Secondary Resonators receive different enhancements.\n\n[Echo Level]\n1. Earn Echo Level EXP by clearing specific Nodes.\n2. Leveling up your Echoes increases certain stats.",
+  "HelpText_711_Title": "Team and Echo Levels",
+  "HelpText_712_Content": "Xiangli Yao cast <color=Highlight>Resonance Skill: Decipher</color> to enter the <color=Highlight>Intuition</color>. When Xiangli Yao is in the <color=Highlight>Intuition</color> state, <color=Highlight>hold Normal Attack</color> to consume <color=Highlight>Performance Capacity</color> and cast <color=Highlight>Heavy Attack: Charged Shot</color>, dealing <color=Thunder>Electro DMG</color>.",
+  "HelpText_712_Title": "Dreamfield Enhancement - Xiangli Yao",
+  "HelpText_713_Content": "When Jinhsi is in the <color=Highlight>Incarnation</color> state, <color=Highlight>hold Basic Attack</color> to consume <color=Highlight>Incandescence</color> and cast <color=Highlight>Heavy Attack: Soaring Loong</color> and <color=Highlight>Heavy Attack: Diving Loong</color>.",
+  "HelpText_713_Title": "Dreamfield Enhancement - Jinhsi",
+  "HelpText_714_Content": "Changli can cast <color=Highlight>Heavy Attack: Flaming Sacrifice</color> 3 times to unlock the more powerful  <color=Highlight>Resonance Liberation: Heavenfire Dominion</color>.",
+  "HelpText_714_Title": "Dreamfield Enhancement - Changli",
+  "HelpText_715_Content": "When Camellya is in the <color=Highlight>Blossom Mode</color>, remaining time counts down faster and <color=Highlight>Basic Attack</color> deals more total DMG.\nWhen Camellya is not in the <color=Highlight>Blossom Mode</color>, dealing DMG stacks <color=Highlight>Creeping Vines</color>. Accumulate a certain stacks of <color=Highlight>Creeping Vines</color> to cast <color=Highlight>Resonance Skill: Cluster Blossoms</color>.",
+  "HelpText_715_Title": "Dreamfield Enhancement - Camellya",
+  "HelpText_716_Content": "When Carlotta is in the <color=Highlight>Twilight Tango</color> state, casting <color=Highlight>Resonance Skill</color> resets the charges of <color=Highlight>Death Knell</color>.\nCasting <color=Highlight>Death Knell</color> while in <color=Highlight>Twilight Tango</color> deals extra Vibration Strength DMG to enemy targets.\n<color=Highlight>Resonance Liberation: Fatal Finale</color> deals more DMG to immobilized targets.",
+  "HelpText_716_Title": "Dreamfield Enhancement - Carlotta",
+  "HelpText_717_Content": "You can equip an obtained Sediment and press <color=highlight>4 to use its Active Skill</color> in combat.",
