   "HelpText_71_Content": "[Event Rules]\nThe Pioneer Association has picked the Central Plains as the theme for an upcoming edition of <i>Wutherium Geographic</i>. To that end, the association has organized a special survey of the Central Plains.\nComplete Survey Tasks and accumulate Survey Points to secure valuable rewards offered by the Pioneer Association.\n\n[Task Reset]\nSurvey Tasks reset daily at 04:00. Upon reset, any unclaimed Survey Points will be automatically claimed, and uncompleted tasks will expire.\nIf you have any unclaimed rewards when the event ends, you can log in within 30 days afterward to claim them in your Mail.",
   "HelpText_71_Title": "[Wuthering Exploration] Event Description",
   "HelpText_72_Content": "For certain classes of Tacet Discords, your Terminal can consume extra computational power to enhance its Echo absorption and increase your chances of getting Echo drops. It can perform a limited number of enhanced absorptions, and then it will need time to recharge.\nThe enhanced absorption attempts of different classes are counted separately.\n*Cooldown resets at server time 04:00 every Monday.",
   "HelpText_72_Title": "Enhanced Drop Rate",
   "HelpText_73_Content": "[About]\n\nThe Academy is experimenting with a new type of technology rumored to be capable of simulating powerful enemies to help with the troops' combat training...\n\n[Eligibility]\n\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n[Event Rules]\n\n1. In Tactical Simulacra, challenge waves of powerful enemies by using special buffs across different simulation domains.\n\n2. As you complete more challenges, more special buffs will be unlocked to aid you in taking on subsequent challenges.\n\n3. The results of each challenge consist of three parts: Monster Points, Time Points, and Technical Points.\n\ni. Monster Points are earned by defeating enemies in challenges.\n\nii. Time Points are earned based on the time remaining when a challenge is completed. The more enemies that are defeated, the higher the point conversion factor.\n\niii. Technical Points are earned for each successful Counterattack and Dodge triggered. There's a maximum limit to the number of Technical Points that can be earned from each challenge.",
   "HelpText_73_Title": "About Tactical Simulacra",
+  "HelpText_748_Content": "A lucky draw game sponsored by Eekky Logistics. Use a <color=#d19f27>Lucky Draw Ticket</color> or spend <texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity38/SolarSchool/T_IconSolarSchoolZS00Coin.T_IconSolarSchoolZS00Coin,0.8/><color=#d19f27>School Badges</color> to draw a random prize.",
+  "HelpText_748_Title": "Eekky Lucky Draw",
   "HelpText_74_Content": "[About]\nUncle Fu says that he has a magical item.\nIt's said that this item is shaped like a scale and has a magical power called Chrono Trace that can make people relive moments from their past...\n\n[Eligibility]\nComplete the prerequisite side quest Scale of Past.\nThe side quest Scale of Past unlocks after completing the main quests Jinzhou Rising: Thaw of Eons.\n\n[Event Rules]\nExplore areas according to the clues to collect the scattered Chrono Traces.\nCollect all the Chrono Traces to receive Astrites and other rewards.\nMore Chrono Traces will be available for collection in other areas in the future...\n\nThis system is permanently available, and Traces of Mt. Firmament can still be accessed via Trace Scale after the event ends.",
   "HelpText_74_Title": "About \"Traces of Mt. Firmament\"",
   "HelpText_75_Content": "[About]\nUncle Fu says that he has a magical item.\nIt's said that this item is shaped like a scale and has a magical power called Chrono Trace that can make people relive moments from their past...\n\n[Event Rules]\nExplore areas according to the clues to collect the scattered Chrono Traces.\nCollect all the Chrono Traces to receive Astrites and other rewards.\nMore Chrono Traces will be available for collection in other areas in the future...",
   "HelpText_75_Title": "About Scale of Past",
-  "HelpText_76_Content": "[Memetic Tuning]\nBefore exploring the Illusive Realm, Memetic Tuning can be selected to adjust the difficulty of the exploration and the reward rate (Memetic Tuning can only be used in Difficulty Ⅳ, V, and VI).\nMemetic Tuning affects Resonators' combat experience and enemies' abilities in the upcoming Illusive Realm exploration. The reward rate will be applied to the Illusive Specimens and Memory Points obtained after completing the upcoming exploration.\n\nReverie Memes: Reduce the overall difficulty and the reward rate of the upcoming exploration.\nNightmare Memes: Increase the overall difficulty and the reward rate of the upcoming exploration.",
+  "HelpText_76_Content": "[Memetic Tuning]\nBefore exploring the Illusive Realm, Memetic Tuning can be selected to adjust the difficulty of the exploration and the reward rate (Memetic Tuning can only be used in Difficulty Ⅳ, Ⅴ, and Ⅵ).\nMemetic Tuning affects Resonators' combat experience and enemies' abilities in the upcoming Illusive Realm exploration. The reward rate will be applied to the Illusive Specimens and Memory Points obtained after completing the upcoming exploration.\n\nReverie Memes: Reduce the overall difficulty and the reward rate of the upcoming exploration.\nNightmare Memes: Increase the overall difficulty and the reward rate of the upcoming exploration.",
   "HelpText_76_Title": "About Memetic Tuning",
   "HelpText_77_Content": "[About]\nComplete the Lollo Campaigns proposed by Maji, the administrator of Jinzhou Lollo Logistics, to claim your Lollo Stamps—a gift of gratitude from Lollo Logistics.\nLollo Stamps can be exchanged for a Lollo Helper special delivery.\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n[Event Rules]\nDuring the event, you can complete Lollo Campaigns once per day to obtain a set number of Lollo Stamps.\nEach Lollo Stamp can be exchanged for a Lollo Helper special delivery.\nThere are 3 Inventories for the Lollo Helper special deliveries. Once you collect all deliveries in an Inventory, the next Inventory will be unlocked.\nIf you win the Lollo Express special delivery service, you can claim all deliveries in the current Inventory.\nAfter the event ends, the unfinished Lollo Campaigns will not be available, and all the remaining Lollo Stamps will be recycled.",
