+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_14_Desc": "You and Namipon encounter the first foe on your journey: <color=#d19f27>\"Maid Namipon\"</color>, a vision of grace and beauty whose singing can banish all the world's troubles. It's about to unleash its ultimate move, \"Namipon's Leitmotif.\" You decide to...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_15_Desc": "\"After all those trials, you and Regular Namipon must be inseparable by now.\" To your surprise, Chisa and her Namipon step forward to challenge you. With an air utterly unlike her usual self, she sweeps back her long hair, strikes a cool pose, and declares, \"I am <color=#d19f27>Gym Leader Kuchiba Chisa</color>. Trainer {PlayerName}, show me what you've got!\"",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_16_Desc": "You and <color=#d19f27>Chisa</color> arrive at the shop you'd arranged to visit, only to find <color=#d19f27>the door firmly shut</color>. No one answers your knocks, and the owner won't pick up the phone. \nYou'll have to find another way to get the supplies you need for the event...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_17_Desc": "You and <color=#d19f27>Chisa</color> present your proposal to a major shopping mall chain. After reviewing it, the representative offers to sponsor only <color=#d19f27>half the supplies</color> you've requested. \nWith these supplies crucial to your upcoming events, it's time to negotiate...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_18_Desc": "Officer <color=#d19f27>Xiangli Yao</color> hands you a club application from a student group called the\"Multi-Turret Club,\" dedicated to researching and building combat robots. Looking a little conflicted, he leaves it to you to decide <color=#d19f27>whether to approve</color> the application. \nThe Student Council is here to serve the students. The call is yours.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_19_Desc": "Your on-campus safety talk has hit a snag: far more students have shown up than the venue can accommodate. At this rate, the safety talk itself is becoming a safety hazard! <color=#d19f27>Changli</color>, the main speaker, gives you a pointed look. Unless someone steps in, the event will have to be canceled.\nThink fast. You're the only one who can <color=#d19f27>save the event</color>!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_20_Desc": "Club Leader <color=#d19f27>Ciaccona</color> has a problem: two percussionists have called in sick with colds. With a crucial part of the ensemble missing, the Orchestra Club can't hold its <color=#d19f27>ensemble rehearsal</color> as planned. \nFortunately, you've already got an idea...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_21_Desc": "The Vocal Music Club and Dance Club are at odds over <color=#d19f27>the same rehearsal space</color>. You and Cartethyia rush to the scene. Both clubs need the venue to rehearse their new performances, and neither will budge.\nWhen talking gets you nowhere, <color=#d19f27>Cartethyia</color> silently rolls up her sleeves. You stop her and assure her you've got a plan...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_22_Desc": "On a clear day, you head to the coast with your painting supplies. Beneath the cloudless sky, blue waves roll in the breeze, sunlight glinting off the water like scattered silver. Beachgoers bustle nearby as waterbirds skim low over the shore. All is calm and peaceful.\nThe scene sparks your inspiration. You unfurl your canvas and <color=#d19f27>raise your brush</color>...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_3_Desc": "You get caught daydreaming in <color=#d19f27>Miss Verina's</color> math class and are promptly \"volunteered\" to solve a problem at the board: 3×4=?\nLooks easy enough, but who knows? There could be a trick. Stay sharp! Just then, a helpful classmate in the audience holds up a sign with the answer: <color=#d19f27>12</color>!\nSo, the answer is—",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_4_Desc": "You're lost in the symphony's beautiful melodies when someone tugs at your sleeve... You follow the tug and look down. Wait, why is there a capybara floating in midair?! And it's wearing a white bow tie! It blinks at you and asks, <color=#d19f27>\"Dear guest, can you sing 'Namipon's Leitmotif'?\"</color>",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_5_Desc": "A <color=#d19f27>crumpled note</color> sails in a perfect arc from the back row and lands on your desk. Inside is a single question: <color=#d19f27>\"What's the answer to the multiple-choice questions?\"</color>\nYou glance back. The sender is watching you with barely concealed hope. Rather than endure that expectant stare for the rest of the exam, you decide to...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_6_Desc": "A few <color=#d19f27>rough-looking customers</color> have barged into the store. Four of them, and none look friendly. The burly man in front pulls three apples from his shopping basket, slams them onto the counter, and growls, \"You! <color=#d19f27>Split these three apples evenly among us four brothers</color>! Can't do it? Then I ain't paying a cent!\"",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_7_Desc": "You stop and try opening one of the classroom doors. Then...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_8_Desc": "Something clatters to the floor. You tighten your grip on your flashlight and slowly approach the corner...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_9_Desc": "A \"ghost\" in an old school uniform peeks out from a cabinet, waiting to see how you will react...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_14_1": "Regular Namipon, I choose you! Use <color=#d19f27>\"Tackle\"</color>!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_14_1_Fail": "Hang on. Does Namipon even understand that command? And shouldn't you strike a cooler pose when you shout it? While you're busy wondering, Maid Namipon launches into \"Namipon's Leitmotif,\" and Regular Namipon, tired of waiting for orders, takes its paw and starts singing along: Bo bo bo, bo ba bo bo...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_14_1_Suc": "\"Namipon, Namipon!\" Regular Namipon gets the message. Puffing out its cheeks to the absolute limit, it charges at Maid Namipon like a fluffy cannonball. Just before impact, Maid Namipon obligingly keels over. It's role-play, after all, and both Namipons seem to be loving it!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_14_2": "Who says Trainers can't join the fight? <color=#d19f27>Get hands-on</color> and clamp Maid Namipon's snout shut!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_14_2_Fail": "You charge in confidently, ready to pinch Maid Namipon's snout shut. But the moment you touch it, that fluffy fur wins you over! Before you know it, you're stroking its silky coat as \"Namipon's Leitmotif\" plays in the background...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_14_2_Suc": "Before Maid Namipon can sing a note, you dash in and clamp its snout shut! Silenced, it has no choice but to remove its apron and wave it like a white flag. Regular Namipon is so impressed by your audacity that it declares you its Trainer.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_14_3": "Why can't I <color=#d19f27>catch</color> Maid Namipon?",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_14_3_Fail": "\"Maid Namipon, I've always believed in your potential, but frankly, your current performance has been a real disappointment.\" You try borrowing the sort of carefully crafted rhetoric people use to curry favor, and it does get Maid Namipon to stop singing. But now, both Namipons are staring at you like you're the most insufferable person they've ever met...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_14_3_Suc": "\"Maid Namipon, why spend your whole life cooped up here? Come travel the world with me!\" You put on your best cartoon-hero voice, and it works like a charm! Maid Namipon calls off the battle, and the three of you join hands to sing \"Namipon's Leitmotif\" in celebration of your newfound friendship.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_15_1": "Duel <color=#d19f27>seriously</color>—Regular Namipon, use \"Tackle\"!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_15_1_Fail": "You put so much thought into strategy that you call your move a beat too late. Chisa's Namipon strikes first, ramming your Regular Namipon square in the belly and sending it tumbling to the ground, dazed. Looks like that's the match!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_15_1_Suc": "\"Namipon, Namipon!\" \"Namipon, Namipon!\" Sensing their Trainers' determination, the two Namipons collide in the middle of the gym like bouncy rice dumplings, trading blows without either giving an inch. You and Chisa exchange knowing smiles. Looks like the Namipons are having a blast!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_15_2": "Duel <color=#d19f27>in style</color>—Regular Namipon, use \"None shall whisper\"!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_15_2_Fail": "Shouting a move name this grand takes serious lung capacity, but sadly, you've been skipping your workouts. Your battle cry comes out short of breath and fails to intimidate Chisa's Namipon. Regular Namipon gives it everything, but against Chisa's all-out assault, it's just not enough...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_15_2_Suc": "\"Namipon!\" A sharp glint flashes in Regular Namipon's eyes. Fired up by your battle cry, it takes to the air at astonishing speed, as though black wings have sprouted from its back! Chisa's Namipon is overwhelmed by the display, and Regular Namipon bonks it clean out cold. And that's the match!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_15_3": "Duel <color=#d19f27>casually</color>—Regular Namipon, use \"Attack Like You Just Spotted Half-Price Chips\"!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_15_3_Fail": "Nobody can resist half-price chips, not even Namipon... or Chisa's Namipon! Your delivery sounds so much like a supermarket clearance announcement that both Namipons believe the deal is real. The glorious battle devolves into a chaotic brawl on an imaginary sales floor. What a disaster!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_15_3_Suc": "\"Namipon! Namipon!\" Nobody can resist half-price chips, and Regular Namipon is no exception. With a wicked grin, it dodges and weaves through the imaginary stampede to the snack aisle, slipping behind Chisa's Namipon in a flash to land the finishing blow! Half-price chips are the victor's crown!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_16_1": "Visit the shop next door and <color=#d19f27>see what you can find out</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_16_1_Fail": "You talk with the manager of the shop next door, but learn nothing useful.\nLooks like you'll have to return another time to collect the supplies.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_16_1_Suc": "You learn from the shop next door that the owner has a habit of locking up for an afternoon nap. You and your companion keep knocking until you finally wake the owner and secure the event supplies.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_16_2": "Call the owner out with <color=#d19f27>a song</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_16_2_Fail": "Under Chisa's startled gaze, you start to sing. But your singing is rather hard on the ears, so much so that a passerby steps in to stop you.\nLooks like you'll have to come back another time to pick up the supplies.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_16_2_Suc": "Chisa stares in surprise as you break into song. Your voice rings out, loud and lovely, and before long the shop door swings open. The owner, woken from a nap, hands the supplies over to you and Chisa.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_16_3": "Unleash <color=#d19f27>the invincible scissors</color> on the door, together with Chisa.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_16_3_Fail": "\"Isn't this illegal?\" Even so, at your request, Chisa takes out the stationery scissors she carries with her. You make a few passes at the door with them, but they plainly don't stand a chance.\nLooks like you'll have to come back another time to pick up the supplies.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_16_3_Suc": "\"Isn't this illegal?\" Even so, at your request, Chisa takes out the scissors she carries with her. Just as the two of you are about to go at the door, the owner opens it, a little startled, and hands over the supplies.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_17_1": "Make <color=#d19f27>a concession</color> and promote the mall more at the event.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_17_1_Fail": "You offer the mall extra publicity at the event, but when it comes to specifics, you draw a blank.\nThey shake their head and turn down your request.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_17_1_Suc": "You offer the mall extra publicity at the event and walk the person in charge through the details one by one.\nMoved by your sincerity, they agree to the partnership.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_17_2": "\"If you won't, someone else will.\"",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_17_2_Fail": "You stand firm, but the person in charge sees through your bluff.\nThey shake their head and turn down your request.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_17_2_Suc": "You don't budge: the full amount, or you take your business elsewhere.\nAfter much deliberation, they agree to the deal.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_17_3": "Time to <color=#d19f27>show off</color> the Liaison Center's track record.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_17_3_Fail": "You start in on the Liaison Center's past partnerships, but clearly they have no patience for a long-winded speech.\nThey shake their head and turn down your request.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_17_3_Suc": "You and Chisa lay out photos and records from past partner events.\nThey study the smiling students in the pictures, go quiet for a moment, then agree to provide all the supplies you need as sponsorship.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_18_1": "<color=#d19f27>Vet the club's qualifications strictly</color> against the standards.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_18_1_Fail": "The standards... Where was the file with the standards in it, again? Xiangli Yao can't help but put a hand to his forehead and sigh as he watches you turn the Council office upside down.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_18_1_Suc": "You hold the Multi-Turret Club to every standard in the book, and in the end you approve it.\nIt may not look all that reliable, but it does meet the requirements for founding a hobby club.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_18_2": "I need to see these \"<color=#d19f27>combat</color> robots\" myself.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_18_2_Fail": "You drop by to see the Multi-Turret Club's work so far: a robot dog fitted with several water guns. This looks like an April Fools' joke, so you decide to put the application on hold.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_18_2_Suc": "You drop by to see the Multi-Turret Club's work so far: a robot dog fitted with several water guns. Silly as it looks, your sharp eye catches real flashes of brilliance in its structural design. You approve the application.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_18_3": "Every dream deserves a shot. I'm <color=#d19f27>backing</color> this project.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_18_3_Fail": "You sign off then and there. But the rash decision draws questions from the faculty advisor, and the application to found the Multi-Turret Club is rejected in the end.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_18_3_Suc": "You sign off then and there. With the funding behind it, the Multi-Turret Club soon builds its first two-legged robot that walks on its own.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_19_1": "<color=#d19f27>Block</color> the students still coming in at the entrance.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_19_1_Fail": "Obviously, one person can't hold back all the students who have come to see what the fuss is about.\nUnfortunately, the talk is forced to stop.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_19_1_Suc": "You block the students streaming in at the entrance like a security guard.\nYour towering figure makes them think twice, and the talk goes ahead without a hitch.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_19_2": "Show off a little <color=#d19f27>talent</color> at the back of the line. Time to dance.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_19_2_Fail": "Your spur-of-the-moment idea falls flat. Only a few people stop to watch your hasty dance steps.\nUnfortunately, the talk is forced to stop.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_19_2_Suc": "You start dancing at the back of the line, and your fluid, lively moves make the students stop and watch.\nAs far as results go... the talk is saved.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_19_3": "Ask a teacher I know to <color=#d19f27>coordinate</color> a change of venue.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_19_3_Fail": "Your connections are no use here, and there's no bigger venue nearby on short notice.\nUnfortunately, the talk is forced to stop.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_19_3_Suc": "You rush to contact the relevant teachers, move to a bigger venue, and even help point the way.\nThe talk goes off without a hitch, and the message lands even better.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_20_1": "<color=#d19f27>Volunteer</color> to be the percussionist yourself.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_20_1_Fail": "Unfortunately, you're no good at percussion and can't fill the gap.\nIn the end, the Orchestral Music Club postpones the ensemble rehearsal.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_20_1_Suc": "You volunteer to be the percussionist and stun everyone with a natural gift for it. With your help, the Orchestral Music Club gets through its ensemble rehearsal smoothly.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_20_2": "Maybe pick <color=#d19f27>a piece</color> that's lighter on percussion?",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_20_2_Fail": "You sift through a pile of scores but can't find a piece that suits the Orchestral Music Club's rehearsal.\nIn the end, the Orchestral Music Club postpones the ensemble rehearsal.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_20_2_Suc": "You find a classic piece with no percussion at all, and it still gives the other sections the practice they need to gel. Percussionists or not, the Orchestral Music Club's ensemble rehearsal goes smoothly.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_20_3": "Use my <color=#d19f27>connections</color> to find backup in other clubs.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_20_3_Fail": "You reach out to the other music clubs, but a skilled percussionist willing to help never turns up.\nIn the end, the Orchestral Music Club postpones the ensemble rehearsal.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_20_3_Suc": "You reach out to the other music clubs and track down a skilled percussionist willing to help. Just like that, the Orchestral Music Club's ensemble rehearsal goes smoothly.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_21_1": "Help them <color=#d19f27>arrange</color> a new venue.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_21_1_Fail": "For all your back-and-forth, no suitable free space turns up.\nThe standoff drags on, and in the end both sides walk away unhappy.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_21_1_Suc": "After some back-and-forth, you find another unused space and talk the Vocal Music Club into taking it. And with that, the storm in a teacup blows over.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_21_2": "<color=#d19f27>Make</color> a schedule. They can take turns.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_21_2_Fail": "To both clubs, your rehearsal schedule seems unreasonable, and each thinks the other got the better deal. You make a few adjustments, but there's no pleasing everyone.\nThe standoff drags on, and in the end both sides walk away unhappy.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_21_2_Suc": "You draw up a rehearsal schedule based on each club's situation, so they can take turns using the venue. There's some grumbling on both sides, but they accept the compromise.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_21_3": "Wait, they can actually rehearse <color=#d19f27>together</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_21_3_Fail": "You suggest the two clubs merge their programs. Unfortunately, you don't come up with an appealing direction for the collaboration.\nThe standoff drags on, and in the end both sides walk away unhappy.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_21_3_Suc": "After learning about both clubs' programs, you suggest combining them and manage to win both sides over. From now on, the Dance Club and the Vocal Music Club will rehearse a joint opera production here. They thank you for the suggestion.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_22_1": "Watch the beach and paint <color=#d19f27>what the beachgoers are up to</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_22_1_Fail": "A cluttered composition, stiff poses, figures at odds with the background...\nLooks like your figure painting has hit a minor setback. Even so, it's given your painting skills a workout.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_22_1_Suc": "You paint the beachgoers enjoying themselves, capturing that happy moment on your canvas.\nAnd with that, you've finished a lively figure painting.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_22_2": "Take in the sea view and paint <color=#d19f27>the scenery along the coast</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_22_2_Fail": "Murky colors, an empty mood, nothing for the eye to land on...\nYour landscape painting has run into a small setback, it seems. Still, your painting skills are all the better for the practice.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_22_2_Suc": "You paint the coast: blue sky and white clouds, a gentle sea breeze, rippling green waves. Just looking at the painting makes you feel you're right there.\nAnd with that, you've finished a beautiful landscape painting.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_22_3": "Close your eyes, feel the sea, and paint <color=#d19f27>what the ocean makes you feel</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_22_3_Fail": "Deep in meditation, you seem to drift down into the lightless depths of the sea, where an indescribable fish-like shape looms faintly ahead.\nWhen you come back to your senses, the canvas is covered in grotesque colors. You decide to destroy the painting on the spot, but something deep in your mind seems to have shifted...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_22_3_Suc": "You paint the clarity of sea and sky, the rise and fall of the waves, the rough grit of the sand. The sea breeze breathes on your canvas.\nAnd with that, you've finished an abstract painting that lingers in the mind.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_3_1": "After <color=#d19f27>thinking carefully</color>, you arrive at the only possible answer: \"12.\"",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_3_1_Fail": "\"Huh? You need help from the audience for a problem this easy? Have you been paying attention in class at all?\" Miss Verina sighs and gives you a gentle scolding... along with the helpful classmate who showed you the answer.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_3_1_Suc": "Correct! One truth prevails! A problem this simple is no match for your quick wits and sharp reflexes. Miss Verina nods in approval. After all, she only wanted to remind you to pay attention in class...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_3_2": "Show off your <color=#d19f27>artistic talent</color> by copying\"12!\" from the sign.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_3_2_Fail": "The helpful classmate stares blankly at their own sign, then looks just as blankly back up at you. Clearly, the \"!\" was only there for emphasis.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_3_2_Suc": "Miss Verina looks at the answer you've so confidently written (or drawn?) and freezes for a moment before bursting out laughing... Not quite the reaction you expected, but hey, at least you've turned getting caught daydreaming into a laugh. That's a win!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_3_3": "<color=#d19f27>Apply your Knowledge</color> to calculate the factorial. The answer is\"479001600.\"",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_3_3_Fail": "Impressive, but factorials have their time and place, and this isn't it. Don't overcomplicate a simple problem! Half exasperated, half amused, Miss Verina shoos you off the podium.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_3_3_Suc": "The classroom stares at the long string of digits in silence for a few seconds, then erupts in gasps. Even Miss Verina takes a moment to figure out how you arrived at that answer. Now that's the calculating power of a mathematical genius!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_4_1": "Show off your <color=#d19f27>singing voice</color>: Bo bo bo, bo ba bo bo—",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_4_1_Fail": "Wrong, that's not how it goes! It should be: Bo bo bo, bo ba bo bo. Bo bo bo, bo ba bo bo. Bo bo bo, bo ba bo bo. Three hours and fifty minutes of capybara singing later, that melody is burned into your brain for life. The capybara—no, Namipon—will be watching you. Forever and ever...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_4_1_Suc": "As you sing your heart out, the capybara sways to the beat and launches into a bizarre dance you'll never forget. Then, smiling blissfully, it dissolves into a shower of golden particles in midair... Wait a minute, it was just the projection system glitching and playing an Easter egg video by accident.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_4_2": "Let your <color=#d19f27>Feeling</color> run wild! It's too cute. Pet first, think later!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_4_2_Fail": "No such luck. Your hand meets nothing but air—Snap out of it! Since when do capybaras float in midair? It was just a projection glitch playing an Easter egg video. But your sudden grab at thin air makes you miss a beat and throws off the entire ensemble...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_4_2_Suc": "You reach out, but your hand touches nothing. The next second, the capybara dissolves into golden particles in midair... Oh, so the projection system glitched and accidentally played an Easter egg video. To make it up to you, the concert hall staff give you a voucher for an all-you-can-pet session at the Capybara Cafe.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_4_3": "Put your <color=#d19f27>Thinking</color> to the test: this must be a dream. Pinch yourself to make sure.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_4_3_Fail": "You pinch your cheek as hard as you can. Ow, ow, OW! Okay, maybe a little too hard... Wait, this is real?! Your startled yelp disturbs everyone around you, and a staff member kindly explains what happened: the projection system glitched and accidentally played an Easter egg video.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_4_3_Suc": "You're just about to pinch your cheek when a staff member hurries over to apologize. Turns out, the projection system just glitched and accidentally played an Easter egg video... As compensation, the concert hall staff give you a bundle of hay that's supposedly a capybara favorite.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_5_1": "<color=#d19f27>Fling</color> the note across the room and into the trash can on the other side.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_5_1_Fail": "Argh! You put too much force into the throw and wrench your shoulder. The pain throws off the rest of your exam, and to top it all off, the teacher makes you stay behind to clean up for littering...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_5_1_Suc": "The paper ball sails over the proctor's shoulder and drops straight into the trash can. Score!! With the right mindset, a classroom is as good as a stadium. You clench your fist in triumph, and the rush of confidence gets your stalled train of thought moving again. Before you know it, you've cracked the toughest question on the exam!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_5_2": "Classmates <color=#d19f27>look out for each other</color>. Write back with an enthusiastic reply!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_5_2_Fail": "The classmate in the back row eagerly unfolds your note, only to find four words staring back: \"I don't know either.\" They let out an anguished howl, fling down their exam paper, and bolt out the door. Guess even genuine friendship has its limits...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_5_2_Suc": "Your sincerity is unassailable, and your bond with everyone is unbreakable. Clutching the note, your classmate bursts into grateful tears and accepts your answers. You both get the same score, and your friendship grows stronger because of it.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_5_3": "Share the answers using your dazzling intellect and vast <color=#d19f27>Knowledge</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_5_3_Fail": "Hmph, it's only multiple choice. As if that could stump you! Just as you're about to toss the answer-filled note back, the proctor, who's been standing behind you for quite some time, holds out a hand... Busted! You and your classmate are both caught and sent to the hallway to stand holding stools over your heads.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_5_3_Suc": "Knowledge belongs to everyone, so why stop at multiple choice? Fill-in-the-blanks, essay questions: anything you can solve is fair game to share. You snatch the exam paper from the classmate behind you and fill it all in for them.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_6_1": "Put your <color=#d19f27>quick Thinking</color> to work: turn the apples into juice!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_6_1_Fail": "Unfortunately, Roccia's store doesn't stock a juicer. But there's no way you can let Roccia take the loss... With no other option, you pay for all three apples out of your own pocket as four burly men watch you like hungry predators.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_6_1_Suc": "—Ta-da! A juicer! Roccia produces a juicer and paper cups from behind the counter as casually as can be, and the two of you solve the dilemma in one fell swoop. The four burly men, won over by your mind-blowing ingenuity, each walk off with a cup of juice, perfectly content.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_6_2": "Use your impressive <color=#d19f27>Physique</color> to break the apples into 12 pieces.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_6_2_Fail": "You make a great show of wiping your hands, let out a mighty roar, and snap an apple cleanly in half on your first try! You roar again, then... nothing. That's as far as you can get. After a few more fruitless attempts, you finally give up, sigh, and quietly pay for all three apples out of your own pocket.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_6_2_Suc": "Crack, crack, crack! Twelve identical apple pieces appear on the table in perfect order. There's nothing in this world you can't break! The four men are dumbstruck. Who cares about splitting apples now? One by one, they change their tune and beg you to take them on as apprentices...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_6_3": "Speak from the heart and <color=#d19f27>convince</color> them to share the apples with you and Roccia.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_6_3_Fail": "Huh? What do you mean, four pay and six eat? What kind of customer pays and then shares with the staff?! In a fit of anger, the four men swagger off with the apples in their pockets. Not wanting Roccia to take the loss, you sheepishly scratch your head and pay for the apples yourself.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_6_3_Suc": "You appeal to their emotions, reason with their minds, patiently guide them, and earnestly counsel them... Your heartfelt eloquence proves utterly irresistible. The four burly men burst into tears on the spot, each vowing to turn over a new leaf from this day forward. As a final gesture of repentance, they leave all three apples for you and Roccia.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_7_1": "Study the old oil paintings and <color=#d19f27>deduce</color> the clues hidden within them.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_7_1_Fail": "You rack your brains over the paintings for ages, only to realize they follow no pattern whatsoever. Just when you're at your wits' end, an eerie voice points you in the right direction. It's only an ordinary staff member, but someone popping up out of nowhere still makes you jump.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_7_1_Suc": "After careful deduction, you discover a hidden connection between the dates signed on the old oil paintings and the room numbers... By rearranging and combining the hidden numbers, you eventually find a classroom door that opens without a hitch.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_7_2": "Show off your <color=#d19f27>strength</color>! Smash through the door with the force of thunder!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_7_2_Fail": "\"Moment of Resonance! None shall whisper! Celestial might, dispel all shadows! Dispel! Dispel!\" Not strong enough. Try again next time... BANG!! A paper effigy suddenly springs out from behind the classroom door as it opens automatically. You know it's only a mechanism, but that doesn't stop you from jumping out of your skin.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_7_2_Suc": "You gather your strength and unleash a 360° Thomas-style flying kick, smashing straight through the classroom door! Once inside the next room, you considerately put the door back where it belongs. Watching silently from the shadows, a staff member lets out a quiet sigh of relief...",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_7_3": "Follow the sobbing in the dark and <color=#d19f27>listen</color> to the crying girl's story.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_7_3_Fail": "As you get close, the crying suddenly stops. The \"ghost\" snaps her head up and lowers her voice: \"A ghost is right beside you...\" Honestly, her voice is rather cute. But with everyone else screaming their heads off, the hidden actors rush out and give chase. You make a hasty escape!",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_7_3_Suc": "You cautiously approach the source of the sobbing and tap the girl on the shoulder. The girl pretending to cry in the corner slowly turns around. \"Huh? You found me already? And you're not even scared? Oh, never mind...\" Muttering in bewilderment, she opens the door for you.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_8_1": "Solve the problems in the old textbook and <color=#d19f27>work out</color> what the answers are hinting at.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_8_1_Fail": "You work through the problems for ages before realizing the whole book is just \"haunted house notes\" the staff jotted down, with gems like \"what to have for dinner\" mixed in. Then you turn to a page with a horrifying illustration and nearly jump out of your skin. A staff member, unable to watch any more, points you toward the exit.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_8_1_Suc": "The formulas, the numbers, and the placement of the notes all seem to hint at some kind of pattern in the room. You switch on the wall lights in the right sequence, and the illuminated blackboard begins to glow faintly. Wait, it's not a blackboard at all, but a sheet of black paper in disguise! You pull away the cardboard to reveal a hidden passage.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_8_2": "<color=#d19f27>Tidy up</color> the scattered desks and chairs to restore the classroom's original layout.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_8_2_Fail": "It takes real effort to get the desks and chairs back in order. Congratulations! You've just tidied away the entire horror scene the staff painstakingly set up. \"Thanks for your hard work,\" a weary voice says beside you. The staff member quietly puts everything back the way it was, then simply points you toward the hidden exit.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_8_2_Suc": "You hurry to clear away the desks and chairs someone deliberately scattered in your path. As the last desk slides into place, the arrows on the floor connect into one unbroken trail. So the exit's direction was hidden right under your nose all along! You follow the arrows to the blackboard and discover that it's nothing but a sheet of black paper. You pull away the cardboard and find the hidden passage.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_8_3": "<color=#d19f27>Study</color> the classroom's layout and look for a hidden mechanism.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_8_3_Fail": "You carefully analyze the classroom's layout, only to find the design is more random than you imagined. While you're thinking, the projector overhead suddenly flicks on, and a giant ghostly face appears out of nowhere! You jump in fright, and the staff member, seeing your reaction, has no choice but to point you toward the exit.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_8_3_Suc": "After surveying the classroom, you follow the sound of a tape recorder and pinpoint the real mechanism. Sure enough, there's a hidden button by the podium. The instant you press it, all the lights in the classroom come on. The blackboard begins to glow faintly. Turns out it's just a sheet of black paper in disguise! You pull away the cardboard and step into the hidden passage.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_9_1": "<color=#d19f27>Watch</color> the\"ghost\" closely, figure out its movements, and find an opening.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_9_1_Fail": "You stare at the \"ghost\" for a long time, but its movements make no sense to you. Worse, you've missed your best chance to run! The ghost suddenly darts out from the side and reaches for you with a sinister hand... All you can do is beat a hasty retreat down the corridor.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_9_1_Suc": "You quickly catch on to the ghost's rhythm. Just before it closes in again, you slip past it a step ahead of time. The ghost lunges at empty air, and even the staff member playing it can't help bursting out laughing. With that, you make it safely through the corridor.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_9_2": "<color=#d19f27>Copy</color> the\"ghost's\" moves and dance along.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_9_2_Fail": "You do your best to mimic the \"ghost's\" movements, but you can't quite get the hang of it. Instead, you end up looking stiff as a board. The ghost freezes for a few seconds, then takes a step back... Even the staff member seems at a loss for how to respond to your moves, so they simply point you toward the corridor's exit.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_9_2_Suc": "You strike the exact same over-the-top pose as the ghost. Two \"ghosts\" stare at each other in the corridor, neither saying a word. The staff member is a trained professional who rarely breaks character, unless they just can't help themselves. You pass through the corridor to the sound of laughter.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_9_3": "<color=#d19f27>Calm</color> the\"ghost\" down and have a heart-to-heart.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_9_3_Fail": "You attempt a genuine conversation, but your ghost is, after all, a staff member whose job is to scare people. Faced with your earnest questions, they have absolutely no idea how to respond. After an awkward silence, the \"ghost\" dutifully delivers the scare as scripted, then resignedly shows you out of the corridor.",
+  "SolarSchoolEventCheck_Opt_9_3_Suc": "You start chatting with the \"ghost.\" That's clearly not the reaction the staff member expected. They freeze for a beat, then roll with it, quickly getting into character and improvising right along with you. Before long, you're strolling through the corridor in a surprisingly relaxed and friendly atmosphere.",
+  "SolarSchoolFes_lotterydesc": "A special scratch-off game sponsored by Eekky Logistics. Use a <color=#d19f27>Lucky Draw Ticket</color> or spend <texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity38/SolarSchool/T_IconSolarSchoolZS00Coin.T_IconSolarSchoolZS00Coin,0.8/><color=#d19f27>School Badges</color> to draw a random prize. Each draw has a chance to trigger a mechanism that awards multiple prizes at once.",
+  "SolarSchoolFes_lotteryname": "Eekky!? Special Scratch-Off",
+  "SolarSchoolFes_lotteryname2": "Eekky!? Lucky Draw",
+  "SolarSchoolForumHead": "SOLAR-X.net",
+  "SolarSchoolForumTitle_Apr": "Does nobody else think our school store is really mysterious?",
+  "SolarSchoolForumTitle_June": "A lesson learned the hard way.  I hope you never have to go through this kind of heartbreak...",
+  "SolarSchoolForumTitle_June_Acquisition": "Celestial Steed Corp changes its acquisition strategy. A new investment direction?",
+  "SolarSchoolForumTitle_March1": "Genuine question, why all the fuss on day one?",
+  "SolarSchoolForumTitle_May": "Did I join a student organization or sign up to build the whole school?!",
+  "SolarSchoolForumTitle_May_VideoCompany": "Help! What's going on with that video production company?",
+  "SolarSchoolForumTitle_Oct": "I'm calling it. There are ghosts at this school.",
+  "SolarSchoolForumTitle_Sept_Flk": "BREAKING!!! The uninvited guest at the school store turns out to be...",
+  "SolarSchoolForumTitle_Sept_Qualifier": "Of all years, we get the very first Nationals special elimination round...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Apr1": "Every time I see that giant building with just one tiny girl minding the store inside, it feels so unreal...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Apr2": "I know, right?! <color=#9d7710>Roccia</color> is SO cute! She's like a little cupcake!! An absolute sweetheart!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Apr3": "The school forum isn't a lawless zone. Watch what you post. The forum admin is watching you...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Apr4": "Wait, our school forum has an admin? I thought it was run by a bot, like the Student Council's website portal...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Apr5": "Roccia isn't a case of \"child labor,\" guys. She told me her grandparents run the <color=#9d7710>school store</color>, and she's just pitching in to help out. She still goes to class and everything!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Apr6": "Aww, I told you Roccia is the best, but nobody believed me... If you <color=#9d7710>get into her good graces</color>, she'll even give you a <color=#9d7710>discount</color>! Friends get friend prices!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Apr7": "YES!! And sometimes there are new arrivals you can only get if you're friends with her!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Apr8": "Get into Roccia's good graces... get discounts... and access to new arrivals... Noted.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Apr9": "Don't forget to support Roccia's store, everyone! She really does love everyone at school!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June1": "Ugh, Changli politely turned down the thank-you gift I gave her. Any advice, guys?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June10": "Just a guess, but <color=#9d7710>Changli</color> has that refined, tea-and-Weiqi kind of vibe about her. OP, hear me out... <color=#9d7710>tea</color>?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June11": "<color=#9d7710>Cartethyia</color> is honest, kind, innocent, romantic... I can see her liking one of those cozy virtual-pet <color=#9d7710>game consoles</color>!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June12": "No idea how you arrived at either conclusion, but weirdly enough, both make sense...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June13": "How'd I figure it out? Went for a walk by the sea and inspiration struck. We're a seaside town, people! The ocean is where the ideas are. Get outside and <color=#9d7710>take in the scenery</color> more. You might surprise yourself.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June14": "Don't fall for it. That post is obviously a beach holiday ad in disguise.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June2": "Changli? Honestly, getting turned down by her is pretty much par for the course.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June3": "Yeah, she genuinely believes helping everyone is just the Student Council's job. She doesn't think doing her job entitles her to gifts.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June4": "I asked them for help once, and Changli handled my request personally. She was so patient, responsible, and kind about the whole thing... She's the nicest senior ever! I've wanted to thank her ever since...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June5": "Why not make it a thank-you gift for the entire Student Council? Changli might accept it if it's for everyone.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June6": "Oh, genius!!! Okay, you all-knowing forum dwellers... what does Changli like?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June7": "...You've got us there. Guess you'd have to know Changli pretty well to answer that. If all else fails, maybe go ask {PlayerName}.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June8": "Just to piggyback, but does anyone know what Cartethyia likes? I practiced like crazy and joined the Orchestral Music Club just so I could play in a band with her!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June9": "You might as well go ask {PlayerName} too.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition1": "Anyone catch this morning's financial news? <color=#d19f27>Celestial Steed Corp</color> is apparently rethinking its corporate strategy. Direct acquisitions are no longer its go-to move.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition10": "Isn't it just an \"industry-academia collaboration\"? A partnership is NOT an acquisition! They can't just collaborate their way into owning the entire school, right?!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition11": "Wait, does this mean my graduation certificate is gonna come stamped with Celestial Steed Corp's seal?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition12": "Come on. I trust Principal Abby to come through for us!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition2": "I couldn't care less about Celestial Steed Corp.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition3": "Okay, but what does \"rethinking its corporate strategy\" actually mean? Explain it like you're talking to Principal Abby...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition4": "Chill, go home and get some sleep. But seriously, since when does Celestial Steed Corp need to rethink anything? Can't they just buy whatever they want?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition5": "Basically, they negotiate the terms first! No need to buy the whole company right off the bat. Agree on the conditions, then figure out the acquisition based on how things play out.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition6": "Ohhh, is that the <color=#d19f27>\"wager\"</color> thing they're talking about?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition7": "Something like that. So they want to see if the other side can deliver before deciding whether to buy them out? Honestly, that's way more interesting than just throwing money at everything.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition8": "Now I'm worried... Our school's activity budget these past few years has been stretched thin. And Celestial Steed Corp has people on the School Board. You don't think...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_June_Acquisition9": "????? No way!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March1": "As the title says, who made that huge entrance on enrollment day? Nearly took out the school gate...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March10": "Wait, where did that announcement come from?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March11": "Hmph... there's not a single thread on this forum I can't delete!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March2": "Miiilaaady.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March3": "Whoa, maybe don't say that so openly!! That's the new <color=#9d7710>blonde second-year transfer student</color>. She's backed by the <color=#9d7710>School Board</color>! You want to get noticed and drafted into Milady's \"personal guard\"?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March4": "Huh? There's a \"guard\" too?? That's craaaazy.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March5": "Yep. Apparently, \"Milady's Guard\" gets up before sunrise every single day to run laps in formation while yelling weird slogans. Trust me, you do NOT wanna know what they are.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March6": "Glad you asked. I'm in the square, just finished the paperwork, and by the way, I was there when Milady enrolled. All for Milady!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March7": "Whoa, I don't think he's trolling...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March8": "<color=#e46969>[System Announcement] This thread concerns a sensitive topic involving the School Board and has crossed the line. Replies have been disabled.</color>",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_March9": "<color=#e46969>[System Announcement] All for Milady!</color>",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May1": "Ugh, I was so naive. I thought joining a student organization meant free credits and a boost to my overall score. Nobody told me there'd be this much work...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May10": "Student organization member here. Can confirm from experience that we basically live at school. Also, TEACHER, that reply speed is unreal. How many credits do you get for this?!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May2": "Can anyone relate?! Fam!! This semester has wrecked me. Every time I open my eyes, it's back to the grind. At this point, the school history books should have my name in them. Pretty sure I built this entire school myself.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May3": "You should be grateful. I practically got trampled trying to apply to the Student Council, and I still didn't manage to get my hands on a sign-up form.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May4": "Of course! It's the <color=#9d7710>Student Council</color>! With <color=#9d7710>Changli</color> and <color=#9d7710>Xiangli Yao</color> running things, the experience we get here could go straight on a resume.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May5": "The <color=#9d7710>Liaison Center</color> is just as good, actually. Finding sponsors, arranging partnerships, coordinating resources... You get to try all sorts of things. And Chisa? She's a pro!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May6": "I've scrolled through this entire thread, and not ONE person has shown the Club Association some love?! Grades aren't the only thing that matters for college admissions! Win gold at Nationals with the <color=#9d7710>Club Association</color>, and you'll get a whole lot more doors opening for you...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May7": "Dang, I'm so jealous! Teacher, what about those of us who didn't get a sign-up form...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May8": "Hello. You don't need to join a student organization to contribute to school life. A school thrives when everyone pitches in.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May9": "There's always a problem to solve or someone who could use a helping hand around campus. So don't be discouraged if you haven't joined an organization. Second Solaris School is committed to helping every student grow in all aspects of life.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany1": "Like the title says, they've still got several batches of my video footage, and the delivery deadline passed ages ago. What am I supposed to do now...?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany10": "YES YES WE DO!! HELP US, SUPREME LORD OF THUNDER-TALISMAN MEMEPOSTING!!!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany2": "Is this the company that handles a ton of campus events and promo videos? Our club hired them too! They promised delivery last month, but we haven't heard from them since.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany3": "Uh... is it <color=#d19f27>Phro Tech</color> Games Media Advertising Creative Film & TV Directing Catering Co., Ltd., by any chance?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany4": "YES, THEM! I heard a private detective went looking for someone at their office yesterday, but the place was locked up and nobody picked up the phone either.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany5": "I'm crying. Mr. Cris, my contact there, has blocked me...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany6": "Wait, for real? I remember their behind-the-scenes footage from our School Anniversary shoot. Everything looked fine then. What about the money you already paid?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany7": "No way, I thought we were the only ones getting screwed over... We finished filming almost two months ago. Went through round after round of edits, then they told us to wait for an update. Now we can't even reach the person in charge.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany8": "Guys, I've checked with multiple sources. The video production company has shut down, and nobody's been able to contact the people in charge for days. We can be pretty sure they've <color=#d19f27>skipped town</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_May_VideoCompany9": "If you've worked with them, gather your payment records and messages, and keep the evidence safe. Also, OP, do you have copies of the footage? Let me see what I can do.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct1": "Promise me all of you will go straight home after evening study, or just skip it altogether. I saw a \"ghost\" at school and I'm not okay.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct10": "And the \"mysterious footsteps\" are from the maintenance crew inspecting the old ducts after everyone leaves. They're INSIDE the ducts, so naturally, you can't see them.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct11": "Not convinced. It can't be that simple! By the way, who are you?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct12": "...Aren't you stubborn.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct13": "[System Announcement] The admin has pinned a reply from \"Supreme Lord of Thunder-Talisman Memeposting.\"",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct14": "<color=#e46969>[System Announcement] This thread has been locked by an admin. Replies are now disabled.</color>",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct2": "A \"ghost\"? In this day and age? Those start-of-semester exams getting to you, OP?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct3": "No!! That night I was walking down the corridor and suddenly heard creepy rustling behind me. The bushes on both sides were swaying even with no wind, and these pitch-black shadows were flailing around under the streetlights!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct4": "Shadows in the corridor? Noises late at night? Hang on, that's not in our school's \"Seven Mysteries\"...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct5": "That reminds me! I've heard footsteps at night too! Never saw anyone, though!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct6": "WHAT?! SERIOUSLY?! STOP ADDING FUEL TO THE FIRE!! This is a SCHOOL. Full of PEOPLE. There are NO ghosts! Anyway, I'm calling in sick tomorrow.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct7": "Before everyone loses it, has anyone been using the corridor for an event lately? Some spots at school get used at night too, right? A club rehearsal or equipment repair would explain it.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct8": "Hm? A \"ghost shadow\" in the corridor? Let the Almighty Forum Lord take a look...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Oct9": "The \"strange noises\" are coming from a faulty ventilation duct. It's been acting up lately, and a replacement request has already been filed with the Liaison Center. The \"shadows\" are students heading home after night study, cast by the teaching building's sound-activated lights.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk1": "Guys, big news!! You are not gonna believe who I ran into at the school store the other day!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk10": "So THAT'S what all that commotion upstairs was about that day? They were fighting over afternoon tea?!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk11": "It's a surprise though. Fenrico always seems so cold. Who knew he had a softer side? He's clearly not great at showing he cares, but maybe he's not such a bad guy after all...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk2": "Who? What's the big deal? Don't tell me you met that <color=#9d7710>\"legendary student\"</color> from a century ago.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk3": "You'll never guess... Fenrico! THE <color=#9d7710>Fenrico</color>, the chairman of Celestial Steed Corp himself, shopping at OUR school store!",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk4": "That explains it! I wondered why the whole store was cordoned off that day. They said someone had booked the whole place out...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk5": "Yeah, I couldn't even get inside. But I was close enough to see Fenrico spending ages looking over the shelves. Who knew even a chairman could get hit with decision paralysis?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk6": "LOL, with the kind of money that guy has, there's no way he's struggling to choose. Why not just buy the whole store and call it a day? Guess they really didn't have what he was looking for.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk7": "Hold on, hold on. Fenrico, coming to a little school store and taking his sweet time picking stuff out? Could he be buying something for Phoebe, his adopted daughter...?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk8": "Can't rule it out. A few days ago, every second-year class at our school got afternoon tea. Apparently, it was a little perk for students and teachers from Celestial Steed Corp's new \"industry-academia partnership\" with the school.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Flk9": "Right, and Phoebe's spread was different, too. No dried pickled Viscum Berries, but extra bags of <color=#9d7710>Bamboo Iris Crisps</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Qualifier1": "I don't remember a <color=#d19f27>special elimination round</color> in previous <color=#d19f27>Nationals</color> schedules. Why are they adding one this year?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Qualifier2": "Right? It makes no sense! A last-minute extra round means every team has to redo their training plans. The pressure is insane.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Qualifier3": "From what the judges there were saying, the sponsor made some last-minute demands, so the organizers had to revise the schedule.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Qualifier4": "I guess a sponsor could ask to add another segment. But adding a whole extra round at the last minute? Who's sponsoring this, anyway?",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Qualifier5": "Who else? <color=#d19f27>Celestial Steed Corp</color>, of course...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Qualifier6": "What? You guys haven't heard? Word is Celestial Steed Corp arranged the extra special elimination round specifically to mess with our Orchestral Music Club's schedule.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Qualifier7": "Really? Aren't they already working their butts off on an original piece for Nationals? Their training schedule's been packed for ages, and now they get hit with this. Must be rough.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Qualifier8": "The elimination round's music happens to be a style our Orchestral Music Club struggles with. And yet somehow, all the other teams are fine. Make of that what you will.",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_Sept_Qualifier9": "The Orchestral Music Club's been practicing so hard for so long, and now they're stuck dealing with this crap? Seriously, it feels like Celestial Steed Corp and our school are practically at war...",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_UserName1": "System Announcement",
+  "SolarSchoolForum_UserName10": "Blue Aria",
