+  "SolarSchoolItemName_74": "\"Watch of Starlight\"",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_1": "The photo in the drawer is starting to look a bit faded.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_10": "You still remember, clear as day, how loudly everyone screamed when the results came out. You laughed and cried at once, cheered and jumped around, and raised toast after toast to the win you all shared.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_11": "You know the credit doesn't belong to any one person. Principal Abby, the Student Council, the Club Association... every student who stepped forward, every friend who helped behind the scenes. You all did your part. Together, you saved the school.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_12": "It may not have had a happy ending, but at least you tried. You gave it everything you had. You had nothing to regret.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_13": "The disappointment and the silence of results day still haven't quite left you. But no one said a single discouraging word. All of you kept believing the future still held endless possibilities.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_14": "Principal Abby, the Student Council, the Club Association… every student who stepped forward, every friend who helped behind the scenes—you know that even in defeat, all of you had already given it your all.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_15": "You know, to everyone, it was more than a \"school.\" It was your youth. And once that time was gone, nothing could take its place.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_16": "Abby used to tell you all the time, \"Exams have only one right answer. Life doesn't.\" That was Abby. It cared less about grades than about whether the students were happy at school.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_17": "You and your friends talked about the future all the time. You imagined life after graduation, each of you setting out toward a different dream.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_18": "Life rarely follows the plan, and it can't always be smooth sailing. But at least you found your own direction and your own answer.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_19": "Over the years, you've met so many people. They say the odds of two people crossing paths are just five in a thousand. Even someone who walked beside you for only a little while was a rare kind of luck.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_2": "You came home in such a rush back then that you left your things unpacked and forgot about them. Years later, you open your graduation yearbook again and realize just how much time has passed.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_20": "But even now... whenever you make a new friend, you still go out for hotpot together and throw a \"hotpot party,\" just like the old days.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_21": "And then there's the promise you made to her. You've never forgotten. Back at school, you ate together, walked together, and talked about the little things that didn't mean anything, and yet always made you smile.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_22": "You promised her then that no matter how much time passed, you'd meet again someday in the future.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_23": "If your younger self could see you now, what would they think? Proud? Relieved? Hopeful? You can't say for sure. But it would never, ever be \"regretful.\"",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_24": "Because whether or not your life turned out the way you once imagined, there's \"happiness\" in it all the same.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_25": "So keep walking the road you've chosen. Be brave. Be fearless. Be unstoppable. Keep going, no matter what lies ahead. All of us, every last one of you—may our futures be bright.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_3": "The corners of the graduation photo have curled. The picture has yellowed with age. Yet when you think back to your days at the School, with everyone gathered around you, it all feels like yesterday.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_4": "In the photo, you're packed shoulder to shoulder. The sun was bright that day. Everyone was smiling, eyes full of hope for what lay ahead, and a little uncertainty no one could quite put into words.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_5": "Back then, it seemed simple. You'd leave school, grow into proper adults, and the rest would fall into place. The world was vast. There were roads you'd never walked, and more sights than you could dream of seeing.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_6": "And yet, the world was small, too. You could leave campus and still expect to meet your friends at the gates the very next day. A few classrooms, a handful of squares, a few clubs—that was enough to make up your whole world.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_7": "Sometimes, you wake in the middle of the night and find yourself missing those days. Spring comes and goes. Winter returns. The years slip by all the same. That wager that once decided the school's fate... you've lost count of how many years it's been.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_8": "—In truth, it was a \"reckless\" wager. But perhaps that's what it means to be young. You charge ahead before you have time to be afraid.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_9": "But it turned out all right. No one gave up. No one backed down. Riding on that \"drive,\" that stubborn courage and the most sincere of hearts, you actually won the wager.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_Next": "Next Page",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_Over": "Finish",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_1": "You bite into the cookie. It's chocolate flavor.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_10": "You bite into the cookie. It's black pepper and spicy soy sauce flavor.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_11": "Pero says that with confidence, courage, and perseverance, there's nothing in the world you can't do.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_12": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Wind Chime</b>. A day to share the good things. May its gentle chime bring good news, and the breeze carry your worries away.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_13": "You bite into the cookie. It's egg custard ice cream flavor.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_14": "Pero says the trick to learning lots of things is not trying to learn them all at once.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_15": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Pearl</b>. A day to take things slow. May time polish you into something beautiful, leaving you warm and radiant through it all.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_16": "You bite into the cookie. It's vanilla flavor.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_17": "Pero says the stage is full of possibilities. Just daring to step into the spotlight is a victory in itself.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_18": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Key</b>. A day to try something new. May you find the key to new opportunities and discover a world beyond your own.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_19": "You bite into the cookie. It's pickled ginger flavor.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_2": "Pero says the secret to happiness and joy is being at peace with yourself.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_20": "Pero says you don't have to get everything right on the first try. Life isn't a test with only right and wrong answers. Leave a little room for the unexpected.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_21": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Jigsaw Puzzle</b>. A day to explore. May today's unsolved puzzles fall into place in time, and may all your scattered good luck find its way to you.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_22": "You bite into the cookie. It's honey pancake flavor.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_23": "Pero says you don't have to stand out to deserve applause. Anyone who lives wholeheartedly deserves a cheer.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_24": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Lily of the Valley</b>. A day to wait and see. May good fortune find you quietly, bringing a happiness that's gentle and true.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_25": "You bite into the cookie. It's pink salt and seaweed flavor.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_26": "Pero says... Pero says... Pero, Pero, Pero! Pero is very happy, and so is Roccia.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_27": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Mirror</b>. A day to appreciate yourself. May you see the light in your own reflection and discover a better you with each passing day.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_28": "You bite into the cookie. It's a medley of ice cream flavors.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_29": "Pero says... ahem, actually, Pero hasn't said anything all this time. These are all things I've been wanting to tell you.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_3": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Bamboo Shoot</b>. A day to grow and thrive. May your knowledge deepen and your dreams reach ever higher.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_30": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Seashell</b>. A day for new encounters. May you find a treasure all your own, even on the most ordinary of days.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_4": "You bite into the cookie. It's cinnamon flavor.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_5": "Pero says not to worry about the cracks in life, because that's where the light gets in.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_6": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Osmanthus</b>. A day for diligent study. May every lesson bring you closer to the top, until the honors are yours to claim.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_7": "You bite into the cookie. It's caramel flavor.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_8": "Pero says that as long as you keep moving forward with hope, nothing can stand in your way.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_binggan_9": "Today's lucky charm: <b>Persimmon</b>. A day to look ahead. May things go your way, and may every hope in your heart find its answer.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_kaoshi_1_1": "Your results for the Comprehensive Finals:\nScore: {Score:1}\nRank: {Rank:1}",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_kaoshi_1_2": "Your results for the Nationals Qualifiers:\nScore: {Score:2}\nRank: {Rank:2}",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_kaoshi_1_3": "Your results for the Start-of-Semester Special Exam:\nScore: {Score:3}\nRank: {Rank:3}",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_kaoshi_1_4": "Your results for the Nationals Elimination Round:\nScore: {Score:4}\nRank: {Rank:4}",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_kaoshi_1_5": "Your results for the Final Qualifying Exam:\nScore: {Score:5}\nRank: {Rank:5}",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_kaoshi_1_6": "Your results for the National Music Competition Finals:\nScore: {Score:6}\nRank: {Rank:6}",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_3_17_1": "Sorry, kid! I know I promised to take you to school myself, but a few urgent matters came up over the past couple of days. Now I've got to sit down with the School Board. You start on Monday, so you might as well get familiar with the area around the school before then.\n\nYour <color=#d19f27>allowance</color> is on the table. Go explore a little on your own, and remember to pick up groceries while you're out.\nLooking forward to seeing you on Monday!\n\nPS: If you get the chance, could you pick up some pastries from <color=#d19f27>Roccia's store</color> for me? It's on the ground floor of that ridiculously over-the-top building. Roccia minds the shop, and she knows which kind I like, so just ask her.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_3_17_2": "\nYour trustworthy Uncle Abby",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_3_19_1": "Yo! Up and at 'em! \n\nBreakfast is on the table. Heat it up before you eat, okay? If it's not your thing, there's other stuff in the fridge, so help yourself. It's the <color=#d19f27>first day of the new semester</color>, so I've headed in ahead of you. Principals are busy folks, you know how it is.\n\nAs for you, I've already had a word with your homeroom teacher. Just go get your enrollment sorted, and you'll be fine. It's your first day, so take it all in and enjoy the new place!\n\nOh, and don't forget to find Miss Verina to pick up your <color=#d19f27>Student ID Card</color>.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_3_19_2": "\nYour trustworthy Uncle Abby",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_3_20_1": "Yo, good morning!\n\nMade you breakfast, same as always. If you sleep in and run out of time, there are sandwiches in the fridge. It's only the <color=#d19f27>second day of school</color>, so don't be late!\n\nOh, and starting today, your Uncle Abby's going to be swamped. I probably won't make it home till late, so you'll need to sort out dinner, get your rest, and plan out your schedule for the day yourself. After school, your time's your own. Go do something you want to do! Just don't stay out too late, or I might have to dock your allowance.\n\nPS: Swing by my <color=#d19f27>office</color> at <color=#d19f27>lunch</color>, okay? There's something I need to talk to you about.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_3_20_2": "\nYour trustworthy Uncle Abby",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_3_22_1": "Hey, sleepyhead. Good morning!\n\nWork ran late last night, and I didn't want to wake you by banging around in the kitchen, so I grabbed a late-night bite at Chisa's family restaurant. Picked up some breakfast for you while I was there, too. It's in the fridge, so heat it up before you eat!\n\nWhile I was there, Chisa and I chatted about the Liaison Center's work. What a sweet, helpful kid! A lot of the credit for our school events landing so many sponsors goes to her...",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_3_22_2": "\n<color=#d19f27>School's been going for almost a week now</color>, so if you've got time, why not drop by the <color=#d19f27>Liaison Center</color>? You'll get to know how things work around here, and it might come in handy down the road.\n\nAnd hey... now that you've made some new friends, you'd best pay them a visit. Go talk to them, don't be a stranger!",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_3_22_3": "\nYour ever-so-caring Uncle Abby",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_4_1_1_1": "Yo, morning! It's breakfast as usual, then straight to class.\n\nSchool's been going for a while now. I'd say you've pretty much settled in, right? When you first got here, I was worried you'd have a hard time adjusting. New place, new classmates, and all sorts of things to handle on your own. But look at you now. You're a lot more reliable than I thought! Not bad, kid, not bad at all. Your old uncle here is pleased.\n\nNow, jokes aside, I've been thinking. You'll probably have more and more on your plate from here on out. Classes, club activities, the occasional part-time shift, friends asking you to hang out... If you <color=#d19f27>plan out your schedule ahead of time</color>, it should make it a whole lot easier.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_4_1_2_1": "So, being the thoughtful, dependable adult that I am, I got you a little <color=#d19f27>gift</color>. It's waiting on your desk!\n\nTake things at your own pace, and make the most of each day. Just remember to get plenty of <color=#d19f27>rest</color>, too. Don't run yourself ragged, okay?",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_4_1_2_2": "\nYour thoughtful and dependable Uncle Abby",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_4_22_1_1": "Yo, good morning! Breakfast is on the table, same as always. Eat up!\n\nI read through the <color=#d19f27>School Anniversary</color> event proposal Changli handed in, and I've gotta say,  you kids have come up with some pretty fun ideas! Honestly, a few of them have even this principal excited. Like Roccia's special School Anniversary snacks. I want some right now...\n\nBut take it from someone who's been around the block a few times, if you try every event at the School Anniversary, your <color=#d19f27>wallet is going to bleed dry</color>.\n\nSo for now, <color=#d19f27>plan your spending wisely</color>, and don't go blowing all the cash you've got! Of course, being your thoughtful, dependable Uncle Abby, I've already considered every way this could go wrong.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_4_22_2_1": "What if, say, you couldn't resist the excitement and already spent all your pocket money before today? Lucky for you, I've already set aside some extra <color=#d19f27>\"starting funds\"</color> for just such an occasion. Take it, and be grateful! No need to thank me!",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_4_22_2_2": "\nYour handsome and loaded Uncle Abby",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_5_23_1": "Yo! You up? Sleep well last night?\n\nBreakfast is on the table, same as always. If it's not your thing, heat up the steamed buns in the fridge. \n\nNo classes and no homework? That's rare, so go on, have fun at the <color=#d19f27>School Anniversary</color> today! I've set aside some extra <color=#d19f27>pocket money</color> for you, too. Go enjoy yourself!\n\nAs for school's troubles, leave that to the adults, alright? We'll figure something out. You just enjoy being a kid.",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_5_23_2": "\nYour <b>REALLY</b> trustworthy Uncle Abby",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_5_24_1": "Yo! Rise and shine! Breakfast is waiting, same as always. Eat something before heading to class, alright?\n\nYesterday's School Anniversary was a real success, and the School Board wants to sit down with me again to talk things over. There are still problems to sort out,  but I'll do everything I can to fight for this school. I won't let everyone's hard work go to waste, don't worry.\n\nMore importantly, this semester's <color=#d19f27>finals</color> are coming up in <color=#d19f27>July</color>. You've been keeping up with your <color=#d19f27>review</color>, right?\n\nThis time, finals will take the form of a <color=#d19f27>mock Qualifying Exam</color>. That means your scores will also serve as an important benchmark when it comes to deciding on higher education later. So put in the work and give it your best shot!",
+  "SolarSchoolLetter_zhuxian_5_24_2": "\nYour trustworthy Uncle Abby",
