   "Term151106_Title": "SQL",
   "Term151107_Desc": "When Lucy casts <color=Highlight>Resonance Liberation - Netrunner</color> or <color=Highlight>Resonance Liberation - Old Net Deep Dive</color>, she pulls up a Protocol Interface. She can choose up to {0} different <color=Highlight>Spoofing Program</color> effects from the following list, each requiring different RAM costs. Lucy starts with <SapTag=1>{1}</SapTag> {Cus:Sap,S=point P=points SapTag=1} of RAM:\n<color=Highlight>Spoofing Program: Ping</color>, \n<color=Highlight>Spoofing Program: Cyberware Malfunction</color>, \n<color=Highlight>Spoofing Program: Breach Protocol</color>, <color=Highlight>Spoofing Program: Synapse Burnout</color>, <color=Highlight>Spoofing Program: Cripple Movement</color>, <color=Highlight>Spoofing Program: Weapon Glitch</color>, and <color=Highlight>Spoofing Program: Cyberpsychosis</color>.",
   "Term151107_Title": "Spoofing Program",
+  "Term151201_Desc": "Lily can hold up to {0} points. <color=Highlight>Basic Attack</color>, <color=Highlight>Mid-air Attack</color>, and <color=Highlight>Dodge Counter</color> restore <color=Highlight>Dream Perfume</color> on hit.\nCasting <color=Highlight>Resonance Skill - Reverie Blend</color> or <color=Highlight>Resonance Skill - Nightmare Blend</color> restores <color=Highlight>Dream Perfume</color>.\nCasting <color=Highlight>Enhanced Heavy Attack - Woven Fairytale</color> or <color=Highlight>Enhanced Heavy Attack - Woven Phantasm</color> consumes all <color=Highlight>Dream Perfume</color>.",
+  "Term151201_Title": "Dream Perfume",
+  "Term151202_Desc": "Lasts for {0}s. When the Resonator with this effect is the active Resonator and can trigger Unison Response, each stack of <color=Highlight>Unison Boon</color> on the team increases their ATK by 0.1% for every 1% of Lily's Energy Regen exceeding 190%, up to 7%, counting up to 4 stacks of <color=Highlight>Unison Boon</color>.\nThe active Resonator's Echo Skill Crit. Rate and Echo Skill Crit. DMG are increased. Every 0.7% of Lily's Energy Regen exceeding 190% increases Echo Skill Crit. Rate by 0.1%, up to 10%. Every 0.7% of Lily's Energy Regen exceeding 190% increases Echo Skill Crit. DMG by 0.2%, up to 20%.\nAll Resonators in the team gain increased resistance to interruption.",
+  "Term151202_Title": "Silvered Dream",
+  "Term151203_Desc": "Lasts for {0}s. While this effect is active, each <color=Highlight>Intro Skill</color> cast by a Resonator in the team other than Lily grants 1 stack of <color=Highlight>Dream Aroma</color>. This effect is removed when Lily is the incoming Resonator.",
+  "Term151203_Title": "Cradle Lullaby",
+  "Term151204_Desc": "Each stack increases the ATK of all Resonators in the team by {0}%, stacking up to {1} times. This effect is removed when Lily is the incoming Resonator or when <color=Highlight>Cradle Lullaby</color> ends.",
+  "Term151204_Title": "Dream Aroma",
   "Term160801_Desc": "Phrolova can hold up to 6 <color=Highlight>Volatile Notes</color>. When <color=Highlight>Volatile Notes</color> reach the max number, all <color=Highlight>Volatile Notes</color> shift one slot to the left, and the leftmost <color=Highlight>Volatile Note - Strings</color> or <color=Highlight>Volatile Note - Winds</color> will be removed.\nHitting a target with <color=Highlight>Basic Attack Stage 3</color> or <color=Highlight>Movement of Fate and Finality</color> grants 1 <color=Highlight>Volatile Note - Strings</color>.\nHitting a target with Resonance Skill <color=Highlight>Whispers in a Fleeting Dream</color> or Resonance Skill <color=Highlight>Murmurs in a Haunting Dream</color> grants 1 <color=Highlight>Volatile Note - Winds</color>.\nWhen <color=Highlight>Inherent Skill - Accidental</color> is activated, casting Suite of Quietus, Suite of Immortality, or Echo Skill turns the next Volatile Note into <color=Highlight>Volatile Note - Cadenza</color>.\nPhrolova cannot obtain <color=Highlight>Volatile Notes</color> during <color=Highlight>Resolving Chord</color>.",
   "Term160801_Title": "Volatile Note",
   "Term160802_Desc": "Phrolova enters <color=Highlight>Resolving Chord</color> after casting <color=Highlight>Scarlet Coda</color>.\nWhen in the <color=Highlight>Resolving Chord</color> state, <color=Highlight>Waltz of Forsaken Depths</color> becomes available.",
@@ -308756,6 +324124,24 @@
   "Term700030_Title": "Lahai-Roi",
   "Term700031_Desc": "Officially titled the Spacetrek Collective: Startorch Academy, this borderless academic metropolis trains Synchronists and spearheads research into the giant mech known as the Exostrider. Its name embodies its core ethos: \"to carry the flame of inquiry and ignite the torch of civilization.\" Here, seekers of knowledge from across the world gather, knowledge flows freely, and cultures meet in harmony.",
   "Term700031_Title": "Startorch Academy",
+  "Term700032_Desc": "The region where Jedediah was discovered. It falls under the jurisdiction of Mengzhou.",
+  "Term700032_Title": "Mengzhou Borderlands",
+  "Term700033_Desc": "A specialized ward established during the Federated Cities Resonator War. It treated soldiers suffering from acute stress reactions, combat fatigue, anxiety, depression, and sleep disorders, alongside those who had suffered complete mental breakdowns from shell shock or the loss of loved ones.",
+  "Term700033_Title": "Mental Health Care Center",
+  "Term700034_Desc": "Lily's name for the Somnoire. To her, this place where she and the soldiers could still walk and breathe was the world that awaited them after death.",
+  "Term700034_Title": "World of the Dead",
+  "Term700037_Desc": "The former name of the New Federation. Today, New Federates commonly refer to it as the Old Federation.",
+  "Term700037_Title": "Federated Cities",
+  "Term700038_Desc": "A mysterious train that appeared in the Somnoire. Lily explained it was once a wartime military train. But perhaps influenced by the Somnoire's power, its interior is now unexpectedly luxurious and warm, as if crafted to make one forget all sorrow.\nWhat must that train have looked like in reality?",
+  "Term700038_Title": "Train of Souls",
+  "Term700039_Desc": "A sprawling conglomerate in the town. With real estate development as its core business, Celestial Steed Corp also operates across financial services, commercial operations, asset management, and more. Backed by an extensive business footprint and deep capital reserves, Celestial Steed Corp wields undeniable influence in the town.",
+  "Term700039_Title": "Celestial Steed Corp",
+  "Term700040_Desc": "One of the student organizations at Second Solaris School, responsible for external relations, resource coordination, corporate partnerships, and sponsorships. The Liaison Center gathers and organizes information on off-campus internships and part-time jobs for students and faculty, while serving as a bridge between school organizations and outside resources.",
+  "Term700040_Title": "Liaison Center",
+  "Term700041_Desc": "A student-run organization at Second Solaris School, with the perk of an unlimited all-day supply of coffee. The Student Council stands up for student rights, fosters academic exchange, enriches school culture, provides volunteer services, and organizes all kinds of school events.",
+  "Term700041_Title": "Student Council",
+  "Term700042_Desc": "One of the student organizations at Second Solaris School, responsible for overseeing the day-to-day affairs of student clubs, providing guidance and support for club activities, coordinating inter-club collaboration, and mediating disputes. Meanwhile, the clubs themselves are major participants and strong contenders for top honors in the Nationals.",
+  "Term700042_Title": "Club Association",
   "Term750001_Desc": "An operation conducted by Septimont's Gladiators to eliminate the Dark Tide and its creations within the Sanguis Plateaus.\nThe Plateaus' unique terrain allows Remnant Energy to accumulate, sustaining the lingering Blightcloud hanging over the area, a remnant of the first Dark Tide outbreak in Rinascita. Consequently, the region has become a breeding ground for Dark Tide creatures, where the Dark Tide's corruption continues to spread unchecked.\nAs the confrontation with the Dark Tide stretched on, the Septimontians discovered a strategy to effectively curb the Dark Tide's advance: luring its creations toward the Earthrend Wedge and hunting them near its base. Since then, the \"hunt\" gradually evolved into an institutionalized tradition deeply woven into Septimont's culture.",
   "Term750001_Title": "Hunt",
   "Term750002_Desc": "A type of Tacet Discord born from the Dark Tide.",
